WEBVTT

NOTE Draft cue timing follows measured scene audio and word count. Review spoken word alignment before publication.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.596
Welcome to Resgrid Academy. In this lesson, we will take an incident from

00:00:05.596 --> 00:00:11.192
intake to closeout. Inconsistent call classification and unclear recipients create avoidable re-entry and

00:00:11.192 --> 00:00:16.787
uncertainty during dispatch. We will explain the features, the setup decisions, and a

00:00:16.787 --> 00:00:19.370
practical way to check the result.

00:00:19.970 --> 00:00:25.401
A department adds Structure Fire and Medical call types, sets Responding and On

00:00:25.401 --> 00:00:30.832
Scene statuses and connects its county CAD email feed. Consistent call types and

00:00:30.832 --> 00:00:36.263
statuses make dispatching, response tracking and reporting reliable from the first call. The

00:00:36.263 --> 00:00:41.694
examples in this series use a fictional department and are teaching scenarios, not

00:00:41.694 --> 00:00:42.530
default settings.

00:00:43.130 --> 00:00:48.449
Call types and priorities. The call types and priorities used to classify calls.

00:00:48.449 --> 00:00:52.950
Add the call types your dispatchers use and set their priorities.

00:00:53.550 --> 00:00:58.629
Personnel and unit statuses. The statuses members and units report, such as Responding

00:00:58.629 --> 00:01:03.709
or On Scene. Review the built-in statuses and add your own where your

00:01:03.709 --> 00:01:04.490
terms differ.

00:01:05.090 --> 00:01:11.052
Dispatch Settings. How calls page personnel: by group or by shift, and related

00:01:11.052 --> 00:01:17.014
automatic status changes. Choose whether dispatch follows groups or shifts, and review the

00:01:17.014 --> 00:01:18.390
automatic status options.

00:01:18.990 --> 00:01:24.633
Email and CAD call intake. Create calls automatically from CAD, paging or email

00:01:24.633 --> 00:01:30.276
dispatches. Choose your CAD or paging format and connect the mailbox that receives

00:01:30.276 --> 00:01:30.710
dispatches.

00:01:31.310 --> 00:01:36.889
Run cards and recommendations. Recommended resources for each call type or area. Build

00:01:36.889 --> 00:01:41.610
run cards for your most common calls, then turn on recommendations.

00:01:42.210 --> 00:01:47.514
Calls. Active calls and their dispatch status. Collect your call types, the statuses

00:01:47.514 --> 00:01:52.818
members report while responding, and the details of any CAD or paging system

00:01:52.818 --> 00:01:54.450
that should create calls.

00:01:55.050 --> 00:02:00.081
New Call. Create and dispatch a call. Collect your call types, the statuses

00:02:00.081 --> 00:02:05.112
members report while responding, and the details of any CAD or paging system

00:02:05.112 --> 00:02:06.660
that should create calls.

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:12.603
Archived Calls. Closed and past calls. Collect your call types, the statuses members

00:02:12.603 --> 00:02:17.947
report while responding, and the details of any CAD or paging system that

00:02:17.947 --> 00:02:19.180
should create calls.

00:02:19.780 --> 00:02:24.904
Call templates. Reusable call text and note templates that speed up call entry.

00:02:24.904 --> 00:02:30.028
Collect your call types, the statuses members report while responding, and the details

00:02:30.028 --> 00:02:33.970
of any CAD or paging system that should create calls.

00:02:34.570 --> 00:02:39.580
Check-in timers. Timers that remind responders on a call to check in, with

00:02:39.580 --> 00:02:44.590
escalation when they do not. Collect your call types, the statuses members report

00:02:44.590 --> 00:02:49.599
while responding, and the details of any CAD or paging system that should

00:02:49.599 --> 00:02:50.370
create calls.

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:56.181
Text call intake and commands. Create calls and accept member commands by text

00:02:56.181 --> 00:03:01.391
message. Collect your call types, the statuses members report while responding, and the

00:03:01.391 --> 00:03:05.800
details of any CAD or paging system that should create calls.

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:11.395
Call Settings. The mailbox and format used to import calls from CAD or

00:03:11.395 --> 00:03:16.389
paging email. Collect your call types, the statuses members report while responding, and

00:03:16.389 --> 00:03:21.000
the details of any CAD or paging system that should create calls.

00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:27.941
For the training scenario, work in this order. Step 1. Configure call types,

00:03:27.941 --> 00:03:34.282
priorities, and response statuses. Step 2. Create a training call, confirm its map

00:03:34.282 --> 00:03:40.623
location, and choose recipients. Step 3. Review response progress, close the training call,

00:03:40.623 --> 00:03:43.550
and find it in archived calls.

00:03:44.150 --> 00:03:50.229
Now verify the result. Check the saved call details and intended recipients. Use

00:03:50.229 --> 00:03:56.308
a controlled communication test to evaluate delivery separately from the saved dispatch. A

00:03:56.308 --> 00:04:02.386
common problem to watch for: Run-card recommendations require review. Shift routing, unit crew

00:04:02.386 --> 00:04:07.530
routing, group routing, and automatic status changes can affect different people.

00:04:08.130 --> 00:04:13.889
Your practice task is simple. Create a Medical training call for Station 1.

00:04:13.889 --> 00:04:19.647
Confirm the location, recipients, status transitions, closeout, and archived record. Record the result,

00:04:19.647 --> 00:04:25.406
who owns the follow-up, and when it should be reviewed. Use the linked

00:04:25.406 --> 00:04:28.950
feature scripts for the detailed screen recording plan.

